# GKI KMI/ABI compliance: stack protector note
#
# HISTORY (kept for reference, do not re-add config lines here):
#   CONFIG_STACKPROTECTOR_PER_TASK is def_bool y on arm64 whenever the
#   compiler supports -mstack-protector-guard=sysreg (clang >= 17, GCC >= 12.2).
#   That mode made arch/arm64/kernel/process.c omit the classic global canary
#   (EXPORT_SYMBOL(__stack_chk_guard) was #if !defined(...PER_TASK)), so
#   __stack_chk_guard disappeared from ksymtab and the GKI ABI check failed:
#     ERROR: Differences between ksymtab and symbol list detected!
#     Symbols missing from ksymtab: __stack_chk_guard
#
# RESOLVED IN THE KERNEL SOURCE (CloudFox ack-lts):
#   "arm64: stackprotector: always export boot-randomized __stack_chk_guard"
#   - process.c now always defines+exports __stack_chk_guard under
#     CONFIG_STACKPROTECTOR (not just when PER_TASK is off).
#   - boot_init_stack_canary() always seeds it with the boot-randomized
#     canary, so the ABI export carries the same value as the non-per-task
#     build.
#   - CONFIG_STACKPROTECTOR_PER_TASK stays inactive; the compiler still
#     obtains the guard from current->stack_canary via sp_el0.
#
# A defconfig pin (`# CONFIG_STACKPROTECTOR_PER_TASK is not set`) was proven
# ineffective: kconfig ignores is-not-set overrides for prompt-less def_bool
# symbols, and self-heal-config's savedefconfig rewrite drops it. Do NOT
# attempt that approach again.
